{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c61b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a071ed-bbd8-7c21-9056-abcb50bf3e45"},"sequence":360,"recorded_at":1780531400000715,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2841f564-c38e-49ec-9f79-6d62a30047ae","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2841f564-c38e-49ec-9f79-6d62a30047ae","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2841f564-c38e-49ec-9f79-6d62a30047ae"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b71f4fb0-3503-4227-beec-0e2e0166fa5b"},"task_id":"b71f4fb0-3503-4227-beec-0e2e0166fa5b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b71f4fb0-3503-4227-beec-0e2e0166fa5b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-20-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board spawn --help 2>&1 | grep -iA2 \\\"list\\\\|show\\\\|status\\\\|runs\\\" | head -30; echo ===; task-board spawn list --help 2>&1 | head -c 1500\",\n  \"description\": \"Find spawn run listing subcommand\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"On launch: assigns element to agent name, sets status from role config and\\nqueues a tracked background RUN. By default the public command returns\\nimmediately with observation commands. Pass --wait to block in the same process\\n--\\n    - Task-specific DoD comes from the element checklist\\n    - Instructions come from precondition resources attached to the element\\n\\n--\\nboard task context, FIRST/LAST status blocks, skills, or CLI reference.\\n\\nSafety:\\n--\\n  # Inspect and wait on tracked runs later\\n  task-board spawn status RUN-260320-abc123\\n  task-board spawn wait RUN-260320-abc123\\n\\n--\\n  directives  List durable directives recorded for a spawn run\\n  events      Read durable spawn run events with optional follow mode\\n  goal        Show the active immutable board goal for a tracked run\\n  observe     Wait for terminal state and return event delta plus handoff evidence\\n  status      Show spawn run status\\n  wait        Wait for a spawn run to finish\\n  watch       Follow durable spawn run events and stream watcher notifications\\n===\\nQueue an AI agent run (agy, claude, codex, gemini, muse, or qwen) for a board element.\\n\\nspawn.preferred_agentic_system is an optional provider allow-set. exclusive\\npins one provider; mixed retains runtime affinity when it belongs to the set or\\naccepts an explicit in-set --agent. Out-of-set providers are refused before\\ntask lookup or launch side effects. Legacy spawn.preferred_agent retains its\\nbest-effort preference behavior. Runtime affinity detects Codex from\\nCODEX_SESSION, CODEX_THREAD_ID, or CODEX_CI and otherwise selects Claude.\\nOptional spawn.schedule UTC windows temporarily replace the base provider set.\\nA provider or registered model outside the active window is refused before\\nside effects with the allowed set and a concrete retry step; the selected\\nprovider's ceiling is applied afterward.\\n\\nOn launch: assigns element to agent name, sets status from role config and\\nqueues a tracked background RUN. By default the public command returns\\nimmediately with observation commands. Pass --wait to block in the same process\\nuntil the RUN reaches a terminal state; no separate 'task-board spawn wait\\nRUN-...' invocation is needed. The --background flag is required so execution placement is explicit\\nat every callsite.\\n\\nPrompt composition:\\n  Primary source of truth is the board:\\n    - Task description comes from the element README\\n    - Task-specific DoD comes from the element checklist\\n    - Instructions come from precondition resources attached to the element\\n\\n  Legacy compatibility\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2532,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 633,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
